def group_anagrams(words):
    groups = {}
    for w in words:
        key = ''.join(sorted(w))
        groups.setdefault(key, []).append(w)
    return list(groups.values())
```

The bug was that `key = w` used the word itself as the grouping key, so every word ended up in its own group. By sorting the characters (`''.join(sorted(w))`), all anagrams produce the same key and are correctly grouped together.
